cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CAUSE: Chromatin-Accessible Uncovering of SNP Effects"
message: >-
  If you use this pipeline, please cite it as below, along with the GWAS
  Catalog, LDlink and FlashFry.
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Simeonov
    given-names: Boris
    email: bsimeonovb@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4771-1019"

abstract: >-
  A Nextflow pipeline that goes from a GWAS trait to CRISPRi sgRNAs for its
  regulatory variants. It collects trait-associated SNPs from the GWAS
  Catalog, expands them with linkage-disequilibrium proxies from LDlink,
  keeps the ATAC-seq peaks that contain at least one of those SNPs, and
  designs guides spread across those peaks with FlashFry.

version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-10-15"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/simeonovb/CAUSE"
url: "https://github.com/simeonovb/CAUSE"

keywords:
  - nextflow
  - GWAS
  - linkage disequilibrium
  - ATAC-seq
  - CRISPRi
  - sgRNA design
  - regulatory variants

